1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In the photograph: above: Władimir Trubecki, Aleksander Trubecki; below: Anjuta Gorbaczowa (Trubecka), '''Paweł Trubecki''', Maria Trubecka (Dobrzyńska h. Jelita), and Iwan Trubecki (Michkel), Tallinn, ca 1933. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince '''Paweł Trubecki''' (Pawel Troubetzkoy; August 2, 1879, Bobolice near Myszków – December 20, 1941, Tallinn, Estonia) was a partisan of Stanisław Bułak-Bałachowicz, a member of The Special Unit of Belarusian People's Republ
2 CONC ic in Estonia ("Asobny Atrad BNR w Estonii" http://history-belarus.by/pages/terms/atrad_bnr.php ), veteran of Estonian War of Independence, a son of a landowner and revolutionary, Prince Nester Trubecki. In the 1880s, the official
2 CONC  language of Congress Poland was changed to Russian, whereas Polish was banned both from office and education, and the process of liquidating the Polish autonomy was completed. By 1905 Józef Piłsudski's party, the Polish Socialist
2 CONC  Party (Polska Partia Socjalistyczna, PPS), of which Paweł Trubecki was a member, was the largest socialist party in the entire Russian Empire. Failing in his purpose, Trubecki left Warsaw in 1906, and moved to Łeba, The Kingdom o
2 CONC f Prussia. And in 1914, after the beginning of the World War I, to Reval (now Tallinn, Estonia). Paweł Trubecki got the Nansen passport. 
2 CONT
