2 CONT From the diaries of - Koka Aleksandrovna Antonova (Russian: Ко́ка Алекса́ндровна Анто́нова; 10 [23] March 1910, Saint Petersburg – 3 February 2007, Moscow, Russia) was a Soviet Indologist specializing in medieval and modern Indian
2 CONC  history. A researcher at the Institute of Oriental Studies of the Russian Academy of Sciences, she was a co-author of a comprehensive four-volume History of India in the Russian language
2 CONT
2 CONT Circa 1937 - My dissertation required a knowledge of Persian. I first began studying it when I was exiled to Tara as a relative of an "enemy of the people" (my mother). There, my husband, Turok, who had voluntarily accompanied me 
2 CONC to Siberia, and I met Lyubov Nikolaevna Arronet, who had been exiled for her husband, the Iranologist (ираниста) G.B. Shitov (Г.Б. Шитова), who had been sentenced to 10 years. Lyubov Nikolaevna studied for a year in the Persian de
2 CONC partment of the Oriental Faculty of Leningrad University, but then chose the profession of a German teacher. She took it upon herself to teach me what she knew. Persian seemed like a colorful exotica to me in the remote Siberian s
2 CONC nows.
2 CONT https://jlm-taurus.livejournal.com/186462.html
2 CONT
